  "scope": {
    "summary": "A million instances parked on a year-long timer — standing cost, not throughput.",
    "measures": [
      "what every hot path costs while a large cohort sits parked: an empty worker poll, a claim, a new instance start, the scheduler's sleep computation, firing one due timer, reading an event page, opening the inspector on an old instance",
      "whether those costs are flat in the population or grow with it — the suite probes at several sizes so the answer is a curve, not a point",
      "the standing storage of a long-running deployment: table and index sizes per instance, at each size",
      "how long it takes to park the cohort in the first place (reported, not a headline — the build is setup)"
    ],
    "excludes": [
      "throughput: this scenario deliberately has almost none, which is the point. A year-long flow at 2M instances/year is 0.06 instances/sec; the risk was never the rate",
      "the passage of time: nothing waits a year. The cohort is parked and probed, and the timer_fire probe forces a handful of due dates rather than waiting for them",
      "the storm shape at full scale: firing one due timer against N armed is measured; draining all N at once is extrapolated from it and stated as such",
      "history levels: every event is written"
    ],
